WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.470
Joaquin Phoenix is poised to be the next in
a long line of actors who've become the Clown

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.360
Prince of Crime.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.880
And whether he knows it or not, the Oscar-nominated
actor has been preparing for this part for

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.740
almost his entire career.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.040
Phoenix is well aware that all eyes will be
on him as he tackles the iconic Batman villain.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.740
Speaking to Collider, he explained that director
Todd Phillips' vision for Joker is something

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.060
he's afraid of ruining.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.540
Phoenix explained,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.160
"It feels unique, it is its own world in some
ways, and maybe, mostly, it scares the f---ing

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:31.609
s--- out of me or something."

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:36.140
"I asked Todd to come over to audition my
laugh."

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:41.940
However, not wanting to betray Phillips' vision
and not wanting to betray Joker fans are two

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:42.680
different things.

00:00:43.269 --> 00:00:47.400
When asked directly about any anxieties of
letting people down, the actor told indieWire,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.100
"I could [not] care less.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.600
I don't really think that much about what
people think.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.300
[...] Who cares?

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.520
My approach to every movie is the same.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.180
What I'm interested in is the filmmaker and
the idea of the character."

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:02.839
When it comes to losing weight, some actors
take it way too far, like Christian Bale for

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.840
The Machinist and Matthew McConaughey in Dallas
Buyers Club.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.660
Now, it looks like Phoenix is joining the
A-list weight loss club.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:15.940
"As it turns out, that then affects your psychology
um so..."

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.640
Fans were stunned in August 2018 when Just
Jared posted what appear to be paparazzi photos

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.540
of Phoenix looking noticeably slimmer.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.310
Many assumed the actor had begun the process
of looking thin in order to properly capture

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.420
the typical body type of a certain always-smiling
villain.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:36.000
The Joker is typically skinny with long limbs,
and when the first trailer for the film dropped

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.500
in April 2019, Phoenix looked absolutely emaciated.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:45.060
He's never been afraid to go the extra mile
in his movies, but now it seems there's definitely

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.940
some madness to his method acting.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.780
Phoenix demonstrated he's the perfect choice
for an experimental leading man when he tanked

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.380
his own career for roughly two years just
to achieve a viral stunt.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:01.020
In 2010, Phoenix played himself in I'm Still
Here, a mockumentary about Phoenix's year-long

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.720
supposed retirement and his new hip-hop career.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.520
For a while, everyone thought Phoenix really
had quit acting, but the star later admitted

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.960
it was all a stunt for the film that chronicled
his desperation to get his celebrity back.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.440
While he committed to the stunt even going
viral for a bonkers appearance on the Late

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:20.420
Show with David Letterman the film was critically
panned.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.620
Phoenix didn't act again for two years after
I'm Still Here bombed.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:28.980
Despite the negative attention, he told T:
The New York Times Style Magazine that the

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.460
process was good for him as an actor, adding,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.680
"It allowed me to be bold in my decisions
instead of being safe."

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.440
Diving into I'm Still Here was chaotic, scary,
and pure anarchy and sounds just like something

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.360
the Joker would do.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.400
If you consider every movie that Phoenix has
made as preparation for Joker, then the man

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.680
has quite a bit of experience under his belt.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.500
He's a three-time Oscar nominee, and in all
three cases, he was playing violent, angry

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.000
men.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:59.180
There was the psychotic emperor in Gladiator,
a drug-using Johnny Cash in Walk the Line,

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.540
and a volatile cult member in The Master.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:07.020
Phoenix chooses roles that fulfill him artistically
instead of financially, and the Joker is a

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.840
character with just as much depth as evil.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.520
He's been playing dangerous men on the edge
of sanity for quite some time.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.260
Fortunately, almost all of his performances
have been building up to this moment.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.960
Joker is somewhat reshaping the mold when
it comes to how superhero movies are typically

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:21.460
made.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.240
DC has thrown a lot of money at projects like
Aquaman, Justice League, and Wonder Woman,

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.040
to varying levels of success.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.400
However, The Hollywood Reporter notes that
Joker only has a budget of about $55 million.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:38.480
That likely means there will be fewer buildings
blowing up, but that shouldn't surprise anyone,

00:03:38.489 --> 00:03:42.379
considering both Phoenix and Todd Phillips
have teased a gritty character study and not

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.220
a rooftop-brawling hero romp.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:48.760
Phoenix previously told Collider that it doesn't
really matter about the size of the movie.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.040
What's more important?

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.100
According to him ,

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.980
"There are these incredible characters that
are dealing with real life struggles.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:59.059
[...] There were characters in comics that
were really interesting and deserve the opportunity

00:03:59.060 --> 00:03:59.900
to be kind of studied."

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.500
Clearly, the budget isn't worrying Phoenix.

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:06.930
It might not have major money behind it, but
the actor is far more concerned about story

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.800
and when it comes to quality, that's a promising
sign.

